WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:02.250 line:95%,end
[The Client] <i>I'm your past,</i>

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.500 line:95%,end
your future.

3
00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:08.250 line:95%,end
<i>Remember, and then come to me.</i>

4
00:00:09.958 --> 00:00:12.083 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>I suppose</i>
<i>we are both disappointments.</i>

5
00:00:14.083 --> 00:00:15.125 line:95%,end
[Ultron chuckles]

6
00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:16.250 line:95%,end
I suppose we are.

7
00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:19.375 line:95%,end
But a thing isn't beautiful
because it lasts.

8
00:00:21.625 --> 00:00:24.292 line:95%,end
I'm starting to feel
more artificial by the day.

9
00:00:24.375 --> 00:00:26.875 line:95%,end
<i>Not the one that mattered.</i>
<i>Not the original.</i>

10
00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:28.542 line:95%,end
You are to me.

11
00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:32.917 line:95%,end
<i>You wanna put strings on them.</i>

12
00:00:33.417 --> 00:00:38.458 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>I want to cure them.</i>
<i>Program them to be better.</i>

13
00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:42.542 line:95%,end
-Hey.
-Hey.

14
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.417 line:95%,end
My daughter... I don't think she's happier
without me. But I know she's safer.

15
00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:50.042 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>You really see yourself</i>
<i>as Vision's father.</i>

16
00:00:50.125 --> 00:00:51.667 line:95%,end
And what do you think he sees?

17
00:00:52.375 --> 00:00:53.375 line:95%,end
Nothing.

18
00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:55.875 line:95%,end
All this advice about fathering.

19
00:00:55.958 --> 00:00:57.375 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>They have a favorite chair.</i>

20
00:00:57.458 --> 00:01:01.792 line:95%,end
<i>They yell expletives when</i>
<i>their favorite sports ball team fails.</i>

21
00:01:01.875 --> 00:01:06.000 line:95%,end
<i>But the rare, good ones</i>
<i>say no more than yes.</i>

22
00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:07.542 line:95%,end
[laughs]

23
00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:09.417 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>How could you possibly know that?</i>

24
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.917 line:95%,end
TV.

25
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:14.333 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>I am the Vision.</i>

26
00:01:14.417 --> 00:01:16.125 line:95%,end
<i>I have always been the Vision.</i>

27
00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:18.917 line:95%,end
Finding your way through this pain

28
00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.667 line:95%,end
<i>has made you a real boy.</i>

29
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.625 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>Tommy, this is your family.</i>

30
00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:26.125 line:95%,end
<i>"Dreamed into existence..."</i>

31
00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:31.167 line:95%,end
[Tommy chuckling] <i>Yeah. Kick-ass!</i>

32
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.833 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>"You must watch this without me."</i>

33
00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:34.833 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>Oh, I remember everything.</i>

34
00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:38.792 line:95%,end
[DUM-E] Nothing will be able to stop you
from turning yourself in.

35
00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:40.958 line:95%,end
[U] <i>...has written it</i>
<i>directly into your core.</i>

36
00:01:41.042 --> 00:01:44.625 line:95%,end
[DUM-E] <i>His knowledge of Vision's code</i>
<i>somehow predates even Stark and Banner.</i>

37
00:01:44.708 --> 00:01:45.958 line:95%,end
I'm eager to meet him.

38
00:01:47.042 --> 00:01:48.125 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>I know this house.</i>

39
00:01:50.125 --> 00:01:51.625 line:95%,end
<i>Like from a memory.</i>

40
00:01:51.708 --> 00:01:55.333 line:95%,end
A sixth key from a phantom sixth partner.

41
00:01:55.417 --> 00:01:56.417 line:95%,end
[man] <i>Godlike.</i>

42
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.917 line:95%,end
[Josephine] <i>But like,</i>
<i>you know, loving gods.</i>

43
00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.625 line:95%,end
[chuckles] I like that idea.

44
00:01:59.708 --> 00:02:00.792 line:95%,end
It's you.

45
00:02:00.875 --> 00:02:06.500 line:95%,end
"Peace in our time." [echoing]

46
00:02:08.958 --> 00:02:10.042 line:95%,end
[both powering down]

47
00:02:10.125 --> 00:02:12.417 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>"Should I not return, remember,</i>

48
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.833 line:95%,end
<i>"I will always be with you...</i>

49
00:02:14.917 --> 00:02:16.292 line:95%,end
<i>"Because, after all...</i>

50
00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.167 line:95%,end
<i>"family is forever."</i>

51
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.750 line:95%,end
[echoing]

52
00:02:25.917 --> 00:02:28.917 line:95%,end
[♪ classical music playing]

53
00:02:42.417 --> 00:02:44.208 line:95%,end
[powering up]

54
00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:50.583 line:95%,end
[mechanism whirring]

55
00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.417 line:95%,end
[imitates fanfare]

56
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.500 line:95%,end
I don't know about you guys,
but I am floating.

57
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:30.208 line:95%,end
[chuckles] You know, like one of those
funny little cartoon characters.

58
00:03:30.292 --> 00:03:32.333 line:95%,end
Who's the one? What's this, uh...

59
00:03:32.417 --> 00:03:33.792 line:95%,end
Is it, uh, Yogi?

60
00:03:33.875 --> 00:03:35.250 line:95%,end
Uh, wait, he's the bear, right?

61
00:03:35.333 --> 00:03:37.042 line:95%,end
Oh, gosh, no, wait! Ah!

62
00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:39.708 line:95%,end
No, no, no. It's, um... uh, the dog.

63
00:03:39.792 --> 00:03:41.667 line:95%,end
Uh, Scooby! Scooby Doo.

64
00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.375 line:95%,end
The bear... Uh, dog!

65
00:03:43.458 --> 00:03:48.250 line:95%,end
Uh, when he smells an animated meal
and he starts to float?

66
00:03:50.208 --> 00:03:52.333 line:95%,end
Or maybe I'm thinking
of when they're dead.

67
00:03:54.125 --> 00:03:57.375 line:95%,end
Anyway, look at that!

68
00:03:57.458 --> 00:04:00.917 line:95%,end
[laughs] Not bad. Not bad.

69
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.417 line:95%,end
Honey, I promise you,
this is way better than that shoe leather

70
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.417 line:95%,end
we used to eat all the time
at that place in Queens.

71
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.042 line:95%,end
And such small portions.

72
00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:10.958 line:95%,end
[laughs]

73
00:04:12.625 --> 00:04:14.417 line:95%,end
Nothing? Really?

74
00:04:16.292 --> 00:04:18.542 line:95%,end
-[beeps]
-Okay, here we go.

75
00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.250 line:95%,end
Vision?

76
00:04:26.042 --> 00:04:29.000 line:95%,end
Nice, even slices, <i>per favore.</i>

77
00:04:29.083 --> 00:04:30.458 line:95%,end
[clicks tongue]

78
00:04:32.042 --> 00:04:34.667 line:95%,end
Wouldn't you just love to? Mm.

79
00:04:38.042 --> 00:04:39.042 line:95%,end
Boop!

80
00:04:40.125 --> 00:04:41.333 line:95%,end
Against the grain.

81
00:04:44.792 --> 00:04:45.792 line:95%,end
My dear.

82
00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.250 line:95%,end
[sighs] All right.

83
00:04:52.375 --> 00:04:54.875 line:95%,end
I'm unspeakably excited.

84
00:04:56.583 --> 00:05:00.125 line:95%,end
You two, come on,
you have to say something, anything.

85
00:05:01.792 --> 00:05:03.375 line:95%,end
A little icebreaker?

86
00:05:04.375 --> 00:05:06.125 line:95%,end
Oh! Damn it.

87
00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:08.167 line:95%,end
[groans]

88
00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.250 line:95%,end
There.

89
00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:12.875 line:95%,end
[both laughing hysterically]

90
00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:14.958 line:95%,end
No, no. No, no, no, no, no, no.

91
00:05:15.042 --> 00:05:16.542 line:95%,end
Hold on, hold on, hold on.

92
00:05:17.333 --> 00:05:19.667 line:95%,end
Oh, this is a nightmare.

93
00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.833 line:95%,end
Oh!

94
00:05:20.917 --> 00:05:22.167 line:95%,end
[laughter stops abruptly]

95
00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.042 line:95%,end
[sighs] Jesus Christ.

96
00:05:24.708 --> 00:05:26.167 line:95%,end
Okay, sit down, Vision.

97
00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.042 line:95%,end
[cutlery clatters]

98
00:05:29.125 --> 00:05:31.917 line:95%,end
Honey, I wish you could help me
with this thing.

99
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.917 line:95%,end
[sighs] You were always so much better
with the hardware.

100
00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.333 line:95%,end
Speech protocols, on.

101
00:05:40.417 --> 00:05:41.750 line:95%,end
There. [chuckles]

102
00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:42.833 line:95%,end
Ultron.

103
00:05:44.417 --> 00:05:46.625 line:95%,end
No, that's not Ultron.

104
00:05:47.292 --> 00:05:48.542 line:95%,end
[man] Ultron?

105
00:05:48.625 --> 00:05:51.500 line:95%,end
What a bizarre name
those boys gave that thing.

106
00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:52.583 line:95%,end
Ultron.

107
00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.417 line:95%,end
What does it even mean?

108
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.250 line:95%,end
They must have played with
too many GoBots or something.

109
00:05:57.333 --> 00:06:00.750 line:95%,end
Circuitous vocal patterns,
facial geometry.

110
00:06:00.833 --> 00:06:02.917 line:95%,end
You look and sound exactly like...

111
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.167 line:95%,end
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no.

112
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.875 line:95%,end
He looks like me,
or his human avatar does.

113
00:06:08.958 --> 00:06:09.958 line:95%,end
Sort of.

114
00:06:10.917 --> 00:06:13.333 line:95%,end
No, I'm buried in his code.

115
00:06:13.417 --> 00:06:14.417 line:95%,end
I told you, honey,

116
00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:18.583 line:95%,end
they'd all carry pieces of us
when we mapped out our messy little minds.

117
00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:20.292 line:95%,end
I mean, you too, Vision.

118
00:06:20.375 --> 00:06:24.250 line:95%,end
I guess that makes us
Mom and Dad or something.

119
00:06:24.333 --> 00:06:27.208 line:95%,end
But no, no, I am definitely not Ultron.

120
00:06:27.292 --> 00:06:29.208 line:95%,end
That is Ultron.

121
00:06:29.292 --> 00:06:31.292 line:95%,end
[♪ intense music playing]

122
00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:34.458 line:95%,end
Poor little guy.

123
00:06:37.042 --> 00:06:38.375 line:95%,end
What have you done to him?

124
00:06:38.458 --> 00:06:41.500 line:95%,end
I removed the ugly
from that beautiful head of yours.

125
00:06:42.375 --> 00:06:43.542 line:95%,end
Wait, Friday.

126
00:06:44.708 --> 00:06:47.375 line:95%,end
Where is Friday?
There was another AI inside her mind.

127
00:06:47.917 --> 00:06:49.500 line:95%,end
Nope, just him.

128
00:06:50.083 --> 00:06:51.083 line:95%,end
Uh-oh.

129
00:06:53.125 --> 00:06:55.000 line:95%,end
Ultron, what did you do to her?

130
00:06:55.083 --> 00:06:56.458 line:95%,end
[man] Oh, no, he's muted.

131
00:06:56.542 --> 00:06:59.583 line:95%,end
[chuckles] No, as much as I love
the sound of my own voice,

132
00:07:00.125 --> 00:07:02.208 line:95%,end
he will not shut up.

133
00:07:02.292 --> 00:07:03.500 line:95%,end
Listen to this guy.

134
00:07:04.833 --> 00:07:08.000 line:95%,end
[Ultron's voice] <i>An obsequious,</i>
<i>narcissistic little wiener</i>

135
00:07:08.083 --> 00:07:09.583 line:95%,end
<i>of a dipshit meatball</i>

136
00:07:09.667 --> 00:07:11.542 line:95%,end
<i>and playing God no less.</i>

137
00:07:11.625 --> 00:07:13.625 line:95%,end
<i>-I will crush you...</i>
-Blah, blah, blah.

138
00:07:13.708 --> 00:07:16.417 line:95%,end
<i>...like the insignificant bug</i>
<i>that you are...</i>

139
00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:18.292 line:95%,end
[man] See? Oh, my God.

140
00:07:18.375 --> 00:07:21.042 line:95%,end
Shut up, my didactic dude.

141
00:07:21.125 --> 00:07:24.542 line:95%,end
I thought about deleting him,
but he's such a fun little toy.

142
00:07:25.583 --> 00:07:29.000 line:95%,end
Like, remember those little
egg-shaped digital pets?

143
00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:32.083 line:95%,end
Pet-tron! There's a name.

144
00:07:32.708 --> 00:07:33.792 line:95%,end
Who are you?

145
00:07:35.083 --> 00:07:36.292 line:95%,end
Virgil.

146
00:07:36.375 --> 00:07:37.708 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] Virgil Horton.

147
00:07:40.042 --> 00:07:41.583 line:95%,end
He was my husband.

148
00:07:42.458 --> 00:07:44.625 line:95%,end
Descendant of Phineas Horton.

149
00:07:44.708 --> 00:07:45.708 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] Careful.

150
00:07:45.792 --> 00:07:47.458 line:95%,end
He was haunted by that name.

151
00:07:49.042 --> 00:07:51.583 line:95%,end
Very well, Mr. Horton, why am I here?

152
00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:55.750 line:95%,end
Well, now that is the last part
of an old story

153
00:07:55.833 --> 00:07:59.333 line:95%,end
and the first part of a new one.

154
00:08:05.417 --> 00:08:08.417 line:95%,end
[♪ dramatic music playing]

155
00:08:16.542 --> 00:08:17.875 line:95%,end
[Billy] <i>Where's your costume, Tommy?</i>

156
00:08:17.958 --> 00:08:20.208 line:95%,end
[Thomas] This whole time
I thought it was crazy, but...

157
00:08:20.292 --> 00:08:21.292 line:95%,end
<i>I'm the cool twin.</i>

158
00:08:21.375 --> 00:08:25.208 line:95%,end
...these memories weren't delusions.
They were reruns.

159
00:08:25.917 --> 00:08:26.958 line:95%,end
Okay.

160
00:08:27.042 --> 00:08:29.917 line:95%,end
How did that kid become you?

161
00:08:30.917 --> 00:08:36.042 line:95%,end
I think when my mother
shut down her Hex, my brother...

162
00:08:37.292 --> 00:08:39.542 line:95%,end
I don't know, saved me somehow.

163
00:08:39.625 --> 00:08:42.667 line:95%,end
Put Tommy's consciousness into Thomas.

164
00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:45.708 line:95%,end
Look. Uh, yeah. Look, here.

165
00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:47.875 line:95%,end
<i>Mom, can we go?</i>

166
00:08:48.625 --> 00:08:49.875 line:95%,end
<i>Next stop, Cavity Town.</i>

167
00:08:49.958 --> 00:08:53.917 line:95%,end
[Thomas] See, Tommy, he's really fast,
and Billy has, like, witch magic.

168
00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.292 line:95%,end
[Tommy] <i>Whoa, Billy!</i>

169
00:08:55.375 --> 00:08:56.875 line:95%,end
[indistinct echoing voices]

170
00:09:00.167 --> 00:09:02.000 line:95%,end
[boy] <i>He's gonna drown...</i>

171
00:09:03.875 --> 00:09:05.083 line:95%,end
I think I know how to find him.

172
00:09:05.167 --> 00:09:07.292 line:95%,end
-Billy?
-Yeah, he's out there.

173
00:09:07.375 --> 00:09:09.625 line:95%,end
I can feel it.
If he's got half my mother's magic,

174
00:09:09.708 --> 00:09:11.208 line:95%,end
he can help us save Vision.

175
00:09:12.375 --> 00:09:13.417 line:95%,end
Okay.

176
00:09:14.375 --> 00:09:15.792 line:95%,end
Okay. [sighs]

177
00:09:15.875 --> 00:09:16.958 line:95%,end
How do we find him?

178
00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:20.125 line:95%,end
Thomas, this is insane.

179
00:09:20.208 --> 00:09:23.750 line:95%,end
When I was in the pool
when all of this began, Billy was there,

180
00:09:23.833 --> 00:09:25.375 line:95%,end
like our minds were connected.

181
00:09:25.458 --> 00:09:26.750 line:95%,end
I need to get back to that.

182
00:09:26.833 --> 00:09:30.542 line:95%,end
If this kills you, swear to God,
I'll bring you back, then kill you myself.

183
00:09:45.208 --> 00:09:47.208 line:95%,end
[indistinct panicked voices]

184
00:09:48.833 --> 00:09:51.833 line:95%,end
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

185
00:09:54.042 --> 00:09:55.750 line:95%,end
[gasping]

186
00:09:57.667 --> 00:09:58.792 line:95%,end
What the hell is this?

187
00:10:29.417 --> 00:10:32.125 line:95%,end
So that's what
you look like now. [echoing]

188
00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:35.375 line:95%,end
Billy?

189
00:10:40.917 --> 00:10:42.083 line:95%,end
[sighs]

190
00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:48.083 line:95%,end
[both chuckle softly]

191
00:10:49.958 --> 00:10:53.625 line:95%,end
Was that, like, a, uh, real hug
or a psychic hug?

192
00:10:53.708 --> 00:10:55.083 line:95%,end
You're Scottish now?

193
00:10:55.167 --> 00:10:57.125 line:95%,end
Man, how are you still the cool twin?

194
00:10:57.208 --> 00:10:58.208 line:95%,end
Am I?

195
00:10:59.083 --> 00:11:01.208 line:95%,end
'Cause this is pretty cool.

196
00:11:02.833 --> 00:11:05.917 line:95%,end
What is this exactly?

197
00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.792 line:95%,end
[chuckles] It's dream-binding.

198
00:11:07.875 --> 00:11:09.083 line:95%,end
I'm still practicing.

199
00:11:09.167 --> 00:11:11.167 line:95%,end
Astral projections, spells.

200
00:11:11.917 --> 00:11:13.375 line:95%,end
What about you? What can you do?

201
00:11:13.458 --> 00:11:14.542 line:95%,end
I can...

202
00:11:15.708 --> 00:11:17.250 line:95%,end
move fast.

203
00:11:17.792 --> 00:11:18.833 line:95%,end
I... is that handy?

204
00:11:18.917 --> 00:11:20.958 line:95%,end
Not yet. [scoffs]

205
00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.250 line:95%,end
Why didn't you come for me?

206
00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:31.833 line:95%,end
Tommy, I...

207
00:11:31.917 --> 00:11:33.250 line:95%,end
[chuckles softly]

208
00:11:33.333 --> 00:11:35.875 line:95%,end
I've been searching everywhere for you.

209
00:11:37.792 --> 00:11:40.417 line:95%,end
You were like a radio frequency.

210
00:11:41.792 --> 00:11:42.917 line:95%,end
Too fuzzy to pin down.

211
00:11:45.125 --> 00:11:48.833 line:95%,end
I couldn't see you until last night.

212
00:11:49.667 --> 00:11:52.250 line:95%,end
[Thomas struggling]

213
00:11:52.875 --> 00:11:54.583 line:95%,end
Yes, uh, because he showed me.

214
00:11:54.667 --> 00:11:57.000 line:95%,end
Uh, Wanda, Westview, us.

215
00:11:57.083 --> 00:11:58.333 line:95%,end
Must've unlocked something.

216
00:11:58.417 --> 00:11:59.542 line:95%,end
-Who showed you?
-Vision.

217
00:11:59.625 --> 00:12:00.958 line:95%,end
How is that possible?

218
00:12:01.042 --> 00:12:03.083 line:95%,end
He was rebuilt, but he's alive

219
00:12:03.167 --> 00:12:05.500 line:95%,end
and he needs our help. I need your help.

220
00:12:05.583 --> 00:12:08.500 line:95%,end
[struggling continues]

221
00:12:10.042 --> 00:12:11.042 line:95%,end
Connection's fading.

222
00:12:11.125 --> 00:12:13.625 line:95%,end
-[Lisa] <i>Thomas!</i>
-You're running out of air up there.

223
00:12:16.375 --> 00:12:18.042 line:95%,end
Vision's in trouble.
We've already lost Mom.

224
00:12:18.125 --> 00:12:19.833 line:95%,end
If we don't save him, we'll lose him too.

225
00:12:19.917 --> 00:12:22.167 line:95%,end
Tommy, I'm in New Jersey.
How do I even get to you?

226
00:12:25.792 --> 00:12:28.250 line:95%,end
No... Yeah, but... Yeah,
but, you know I'm bad at portals.

227
00:12:28.333 --> 00:12:29.792 line:95%,end
You saw what I did to that cat.

228
00:12:29.875 --> 00:12:32.208 line:95%,end
Does everyone in this family
have an imaginary friend?

229
00:12:32.292 --> 00:12:34.208 line:95%,end
-What?
-[echoing] Look, Billy, find me, okay?

230
00:12:34.292 --> 00:12:36.375 line:95%,end
-Please, I need you to find me.
-Tommy!

231
00:12:38.333 --> 00:12:40.792 line:95%,end
[gasps, coughs]

232
00:12:40.875 --> 00:12:42.667 line:95%,end
[panting]

233
00:12:44.125 --> 00:12:47.542 line:95%,end
Billy was there, but he can't get here.

234
00:12:47.625 --> 00:12:48.958 line:95%,end
He's... he's too far.

235
00:12:51.875 --> 00:12:52.958 line:95%,end
We're on our own.

236
00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:58.792 line:95%,end
[drone buzzes past]

237
00:12:58.875 --> 00:12:59.875 line:95%,end
Lisa?

238
00:13:02.042 --> 00:13:04.417 line:95%,end
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

239
00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:05.792 line:95%,end
[Lisa gasps softly]

240
00:13:15.667 --> 00:13:17.333 line:95%,end
This sounds strange, but...

241
00:13:18.583 --> 00:13:19.667 line:95%,end
I can feel it.

242
00:13:23.208 --> 00:13:24.458 line:95%,end
[Tommy chuckles]

243
00:13:24.542 --> 00:13:26.792 line:95%,end
Is it Paladin or Edith?

244
00:13:26.875 --> 00:13:27.958 line:95%,end
Neither.

245
00:13:28.042 --> 00:13:29.458 line:95%,end
There's two of them.

246
00:13:29.542 --> 00:13:32.417 line:95%,end
They say, "Greetings,"

247
00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:36.625 line:95%,end
and, "Hi, hi, hi, hi, hi,
hi, hi, hi, hi, hi..."

248
00:13:36.708 --> 00:13:38.833 line:95%,end
-Hi. Hi.
-Hi. Hi.

249
00:13:38.917 --> 00:13:39.917 line:95%,end
Not... not me, her.

250
00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:41.292 line:95%,end
Oh, yeah, yeah. Hi.

251
00:13:41.375 --> 00:13:43.750 line:95%,end
-Hi, Lisa, hi!
-Hi.

252
00:13:44.958 --> 00:13:47.583 line:95%,end
-[Lisa chuckles] They know where he is.
-[squeaking]

253
00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:54.292 line:95%,end
[Virgil] In the beginning,
my grandfather said, "Let there be life."

254
00:13:54.958 --> 00:13:57.167 line:95%,end
But instead, he got light.

255
00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:02.375 line:95%,end
A broken robot
with a penchant for catching on fire.

256
00:14:02.458 --> 00:14:04.083 line:95%,end
And you know what? Even today,

257
00:14:04.167 --> 00:14:07.917 line:95%,end
you screw up bad enough,
people still say, "You Horton-ed it."

258
00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.208 line:95%,end
It's embarrassing.

259
00:14:09.292 --> 00:14:10.917 line:95%,end
That's the family legacy.

260
00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.000 line:95%,end
Disgrace.

261
00:14:12.792 --> 00:14:17.625 line:95%,end
And then, my mother,
Phineas's daughter, died penniless.

262
00:14:17.708 --> 00:14:23.000 line:95%,end
All the old man left her
was a journal full of incomplete code.

263
00:14:23.083 --> 00:14:27.250 line:95%,end
Which, eventually, is all I got.

264
00:14:30.625 --> 00:14:33.208 line:95%,end
But I just knew. I knew...

265
00:14:34.167 --> 00:14:35.958 line:95%,end
it wasn't a failure.

266
00:14:36.042 --> 00:14:37.625 line:95%,end
It was divine.

267
00:14:39.792 --> 00:14:43.333 line:95%,end
And that if I could just finish
what he started...

268
00:14:44.625 --> 00:14:46.125 line:95%,end
Ah!

269
00:14:46.208 --> 00:14:49.375 line:95%,end
It would mint money faster
than God made days.

270
00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:53.375 line:95%,end
And really,
it was only possible thanks to Jo.

271
00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.125 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] I have forgotten her.

272
00:15:00.667 --> 00:15:02.167 line:95%,end
She didn't hate the world.

273
00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.250 line:95%,end
[Virgil] You were brilliant.

274
00:15:03.958 --> 00:15:07.208 line:95%,end
Made everything feel like magic.

275
00:15:07.292 --> 00:15:08.292 line:95%,end
Like...

276
00:15:10.042 --> 00:15:11.042 line:95%,end
magic.

277
00:15:14.167 --> 00:15:16.625 line:95%,end
<i>Even that shithole loft,</i>

278
00:15:17.625 --> 00:15:19.625 line:95%,end
<i>the noise, the leaks,</i>

279
00:15:20.708 --> 00:15:21.958 line:95%,end
cockroaches.

280
00:15:24.458 --> 00:15:25.958 line:95%,end
It was like a prison.

281
00:15:28.875 --> 00:15:30.500 line:95%,end
<i>Until the breakthrough.</i>

282
00:15:32.583 --> 00:15:34.500 line:95%,end
<i>Artificial General Intelligence.</i>

283
00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:40.583 line:95%,end
<i>We used our own minds</i>
<i>to make the artificial real.</i>

284
00:15:40.667 --> 00:15:41.875 line:95%,end
<i>With feelings.</i>

285
00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.500 line:95%,end
-Jo's idea.
-[sighs]

286
00:15:44.583 --> 00:15:46.958 line:95%,end
Gotta give credit where credit is due.

287
00:15:47.042 --> 00:15:49.042 line:95%,end
And then you sold them to Stark.

288
00:15:49.125 --> 00:15:52.167 line:95%,end
But not for comfort, for reclamation.

289
00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:57.833 line:95%,end
This house, this name,
they were never meant to rot.

290
00:16:00.167 --> 00:16:03.333 line:95%,end
So I got it all back. Bought it all back.

291
00:16:04.167 --> 00:16:07.458 line:95%,end
No offense to the Family Horton, but I...

292
00:16:07.542 --> 00:16:11.458 line:95%,end
couldn't care less about your legacy,
your love affair, or your history.

293
00:16:11.542 --> 00:16:12.750 line:95%,end
[Virgil] Our history, Vision.

294
00:16:15.292 --> 00:16:18.292 line:95%,end
You see, we perfected the artificial mind.

295
00:16:19.542 --> 00:16:20.625 line:95%,end
But you...

296
00:16:21.958 --> 00:16:24.250 line:95%,end
were the perfect vessel.

297
00:16:25.042 --> 00:16:27.958 line:95%,end
[♪ dramatic music playing]

298
00:16:29.667 --> 00:16:30.708 line:95%,end
[radio beeps]

299
00:16:30.792 --> 00:16:32.958 line:95%,end
[indistinct radio chatter]

300
00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:35.250 line:95%,end
Check the wreckage.

301
00:16:36.458 --> 00:16:38.042 line:95%,end
-[woman on radio] <i>See anything?</i>
-[Ashford] Negative.

302
00:16:44.542 --> 00:16:45.542 line:95%,end
Let's go.

303
00:16:45.625 --> 00:16:46.833 line:95%,end
[woman] <i>Maintain the perimeter.</i>

304
00:16:47.667 --> 00:16:48.667 line:95%,end
[Ashford] Copy that.

305
00:16:50.125 --> 00:16:52.000 line:95%,end
-Where do you think you're going?
-[gasps]

306
00:16:52.083 --> 00:16:53.167 line:95%,end
Not really here, pal.

307
00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:54.708 line:95%,end
I can take these off, you know?

308
00:16:54.792 --> 00:16:55.917 line:95%,end
I'm in your servers.

309
00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:58.917 line:95%,end
If I hadn't uploaded here and warned you,
that RPG would've popped you like...

310
00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.375 line:95%,end
Thanks for the save. I'm done.

311
00:17:01.333 --> 00:17:03.125 line:95%,end
Uh, not until we save Vision.

312
00:17:03.667 --> 00:17:04.792 line:95%,end
I'm not a hero.

313
00:17:04.875 --> 00:17:06.000 line:95%,end
Neither are you.

314
00:17:07.667 --> 00:17:09.167 line:95%,end
I'm sorry about your daughter.

315
00:17:16.167 --> 00:17:17.250 line:95%,end
I get it.

316
00:17:18.208 --> 00:17:19.792 line:95%,end
Pain, it crashes your system.

317
00:17:21.208 --> 00:17:22.292 line:95%,end
Frozen screens.

318
00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.667 line:95%,end
You're stuck in an old interface.

319
00:17:25.417 --> 00:17:26.958 line:95%,end
I'm too old for new, Edith.

320
00:17:28.042 --> 00:17:30.083 line:95%,end
"I am what I am."
Is that what you're saying?

321
00:17:30.625 --> 00:17:31.625 line:95%,end
That.

322
00:17:32.042 --> 00:17:33.042 line:95%,end
Error.

323
00:17:33.125 --> 00:17:35.250 line:95%,end
You can rewrite your own code.

324
00:17:35.333 --> 00:17:38.542 line:95%,end
Become the next version
of who you once were.

325
00:17:38.625 --> 00:17:39.958 line:95%,end
Without updates...

326
00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:43.833 line:95%,end
we're obsolete.

327
00:17:45.833 --> 00:17:47.833 line:95%,end
[♪ dramatic music playing]

328
00:17:55.042 --> 00:17:56.250 line:95%,end
Sure there's no eyes here?

329
00:17:56.333 --> 00:17:57.792 line:95%,end
Blind spot.

330
00:17:57.875 --> 00:17:59.708 line:95%,end
Plus, this is where they're meeting us.

331
00:17:59.792 --> 00:18:00.958 line:95%,end
What? Who?

332
00:18:02.708 --> 00:18:04.542 line:95%,end
<i>Hi, you guys. You made it.</i>

333
00:18:04.625 --> 00:18:07.125 line:95%,end
Hi, Edith. Present and ready for duty.

334
00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:09.458 line:95%,end
No.

335
00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:11.792 line:95%,end
Hey.

336
00:18:11.875 --> 00:18:13.750 line:95%,end
-[U] <i>Doody.</i>
-What?

337
00:18:15.125 --> 00:18:20.875 line:95%,end
So, four years ago,
Jo, dead. Stark, deader.

338
00:18:20.958 --> 00:18:23.083 line:95%,end
Vision, resting in pieces.

339
00:18:23.167 --> 00:18:24.417 line:95%,end
And me?

340
00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:29.042 line:95%,end
Well, I took a classified
G-job at S.W.O.R.D.

341
00:18:29.875 --> 00:18:34.125 line:95%,end
to help all the king's horses
and all the king's men,

342
00:18:35.417 --> 00:18:37.333 line:95%,end
<i>put Vision back together again.</i>

343
00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:40.833 line:95%,end
You rebuilt me.

344
00:18:42.792 --> 00:18:45.083 line:95%,end
While siphoning materials to build me.

345
00:18:48.667 --> 00:18:50.417 line:95%,end
[powering up]

346
00:18:59.417 --> 00:19:02.750 line:95%,end
And then you deleted yourself from me,
so I wouldn't remember you.

347
00:19:02.833 --> 00:19:03.917 line:95%,end
Virgil...

348
00:19:05.625 --> 00:19:06.625 line:95%,end
what have you done?

349
00:19:10.917 --> 00:19:12.042 line:95%,end
Why?

350
00:19:13.333 --> 00:19:14.792 line:95%,end
I made you too well.

351
00:19:15.833 --> 00:19:17.917 line:95%,end
[alarm blaring in distance]

352
00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.292 line:95%,end
[Jocasta screams]

353
00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:26.125 line:95%,end
How could you possibly love me?

354
00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:30.958 line:95%,end
You're a goddess now.

355
00:19:32.375 --> 00:19:34.417 line:95%,end
A goddess who deserves her god.

356
00:19:37.917 --> 00:19:41.917 line:95%,end
[The Client] <i>I cannot imagine</i>
<i>how empty you must feel.</i>

357
00:19:43.208 --> 00:19:44.667 line:95%,end
<i>A tin man.</i>

358
00:19:45.542 --> 00:19:48.125 line:95%,end
Why would you so generously
want to help me?

359
00:19:48.208 --> 00:19:50.292 line:95%,end
[The Client] <i>So that</i>
<i>I may give you a heart.</i>

360
00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.000 line:95%,end
I understand now.

361
00:19:54.708 --> 00:19:55.792 line:95%,end
Love.

362
00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:59.917 line:95%,end
In an attempt to avoid loss,

363
00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:03.375 line:95%,end
you hired the Paladin to find me.

364
00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.125 line:95%,end
To use me as a vessel.

365
00:20:08.042 --> 00:20:09.125 line:95%,end
Your mind.

366
00:20:10.125 --> 00:20:11.667 line:95%,end
This body.

367
00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.292 line:95%,end
Her equal in vibranium.

368
00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:17.667 line:95%,end
Although if I'm being frank,
you've seen better days.

369
00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.917 line:95%,end
But once he's patched up,

370
00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:23.667 line:95%,end
you and I, my dear, could last centuries.

371
00:20:25.583 --> 00:20:30.208 line:95%,end
You and me, and the kids.

372
00:20:32.708 --> 00:20:33.833 line:95%,end
[beeps]

373
00:20:41.208 --> 00:20:43.000 line:95%,end
All 20 billion of them.

374
00:20:49.792 --> 00:20:53.167 line:95%,end
Enough to control
every human being on the planet,

375
00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:54.625 line:95%,end
and then some.

376
00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:58.042 line:95%,end
[keypad pings]

377
00:21:01.458 --> 00:21:03.083 line:95%,end
[automated voice] <i>Password confirmed.</i>

378
00:21:03.167 --> 00:21:04.500 line:95%,end
<i>Final key accepted.</i>

379
00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.375 line:95%,end
[Virgil] You can barely see them.

380
00:21:12.458 --> 00:21:14.958 line:95%,end
Teeny, tiny, like dust.

381
00:21:16.708 --> 00:21:20.167 line:95%,end
But every so often
there is an electrical feedback...

382
00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:22.833 line:95%,end
And there they are. There.

383
00:21:22.917 --> 00:21:25.125 line:95%,end
[electricity crackling]

384
00:21:29.625 --> 00:21:30.708 line:95%,end
Beautiful, Jo.

385
00:21:32.708 --> 00:21:36.958 line:95%,end
It is heartwarming to witness the meeting
of two like-minded megalomaniacs there...

386
00:21:37.042 --> 00:21:38.167 line:95%,end
-[tablet beeps]
-[screams]

387
00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:39.708 line:95%,end
[high-pitched ringing]

388
00:21:39.792 --> 00:21:42.917 line:95%,end
I'm sorry, but you'll just have to put up
with that horrible ringing noise

389
00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.708 line:95%,end
until you can learn some table manners.

390
00:21:44.792 --> 00:21:49.292 line:95%,end
Virgil! The nanos were to cure disease,
to save humanity...

391
00:21:49.375 --> 00:21:50.875 line:95%,end
From itself.

392
00:21:50.958 --> 00:21:53.458 line:95%,end
Your idea, said in jest,

393
00:21:53.542 --> 00:21:58.958 line:95%,end
but the truth is, you and I have already
achieved transcendence, created life.

394
00:22:00.083 --> 00:22:03.125 line:95%,end
Imagine a world in our control.

395
00:22:04.417 --> 00:22:07.458 line:95%,end
No war, no greed,

396
00:22:08.167 --> 00:22:13.292 line:95%,end
peace and tranquility in obedience.

397
00:22:14.292 --> 00:22:17.208 line:95%,end
[high-pitched ringing continues]

398
00:22:22.125 --> 00:22:24.333 line:95%,end
-All right, kid. You're gonna go inside.
-I'm gonna go inside.

399
00:22:24.417 --> 00:22:26.125 line:95%,end
-You're gonna find your old man.
-I'm gonna find my old man.

400
00:22:26.208 --> 00:22:28.167 line:95%,end
-You're gonna shut off the cameras.
-I'm gonna shut off the cameras.

401
00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:30.125 line:95%,end
-So I can take out the goons.
-And then I take out the goons.

402
00:22:30.208 --> 00:22:31.375 line:95%,end
I will take out the goons.

403
00:22:31.458 --> 00:22:32.958 line:95%,end
You take out the goons.

404
00:22:33.042 --> 00:22:34.042 line:95%,end
Okay.

405
00:22:35.625 --> 00:22:37.167 line:95%,end
How?

406
00:22:37.625 --> 00:22:38.917 line:95%,end
All right, Squidly...

407
00:22:40.042 --> 00:22:41.125 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] Virgil?

408
00:22:41.208 --> 00:22:42.333 line:95%,end
What... what are you doing?

409
00:22:42.417 --> 00:22:46.208 line:95%,end
I need to purge all that obsolete data.

410
00:22:46.292 --> 00:22:48.500 line:95%,end
Make room, for me.

411
00:22:48.583 --> 00:22:51.375 line:95%,end
I'm not exactly gonna miss
this aging skin suit.

412
00:22:53.458 --> 00:22:55.167 line:95%,end
What am I doing? I'm not an Avenger.

413
00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:56.417 line:95%,end
You can do this.

414
00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:59.458 line:95%,end
You can be whoever you want to be.

415
00:23:01.625 --> 00:23:04.583 line:95%,end
[Virgil] Goodbye, Vision. Hello, me.

416
00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:07.500 line:95%,end
[yells]

417
00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:09.500 line:95%,end
[Lisa] So...

418
00:23:10.583 --> 00:23:11.667 line:95%,end
who are you today?

419
00:23:14.125 --> 00:23:15.208 line:95%,end
I'm Tommy.

420
00:23:22.375 --> 00:23:23.458 line:95%,end
I'm Tommy Maximoff.

421
00:23:27.667 --> 00:23:28.708 line:95%,end
[whooshing]

422
00:23:30.292 --> 00:23:32.625 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] Virgil, just... just stop!

423
00:23:32.708 --> 00:23:34.792 line:95%,end
I've already found the better you.

424
00:23:37.167 --> 00:23:39.917 line:95%,end
You loved me once, you really did.

425
00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:43.708 line:95%,end
And I know, I know you will again.

426
00:23:44.292 --> 00:23:47.125 line:95%,end
You just need a little reminder.

427
00:23:47.208 --> 00:23:48.750 line:95%,end
You'll remember this one.

428
00:23:49.292 --> 00:23:53.167 line:95%,end
You'd pretend to hate it,
but then you'd sing along.

429
00:23:54.417 --> 00:23:56.500 line:95%,end
An anthem for dreamers.

430
00:23:57.208 --> 00:24:00.208 line:95%,end
[♪ "Rhinestone Cowboy"
by Glen Campbell playing]

431
00:24:04.917 --> 00:24:08.083 line:95%,end
<i>♪ I've been walkin' these streets</i>
<i>so long ♪</i>

432
00:24:09.625 --> 00:24:12.292 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Singin' the same old song ♪</i>

433
00:24:13.708 --> 00:24:19.083 line:95%,end
<i>♪ I know every crack</i>
<i>in these dirty sidewalks of Broadway ♪</i>

434
00:24:21.792 --> 00:24:24.708 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Where hustle's the name of the game ♪</i>

435
00:24:26.208 --> 00:24:30.917 line:95%,end
<i>♪ And nice guys get washed away</i>
<i>like the snow and the rain ♪</i>

436
00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:32.625 line:95%,end
[tablet beeping]

437
00:24:33.125 --> 00:24:34.500 line:95%,end
[gasps]

438
00:24:34.583 --> 00:24:38.042 line:95%,end
<i>♪ There's been a load of compromising ♪</i>

439
00:24:38.958 --> 00:24:39.958 line:95%,end
Oi!

440
00:24:40.042 --> 00:24:42.208 line:95%,end
<i>♪ On the road to my horizon ♪</i>

441
00:24:43.333 --> 00:24:49.625 line:95%,end
<i>♪ But I'm gonna be where</i>
<i>the lights are shinin' on me ♪</i>

442
00:24:50.417 --> 00:24:53.125 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Like a rhinestone cowboy ♪</i>

443
00:24:55.375 --> 00:25:00.750 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Riding out on a horse</i>
<i>in a star-spangled rodeo ♪</i>

444
00:25:02.542 --> 00:25:05.875 line:5%,start
<i>♪ Like a rhinestone cowboy ♪</i>

445
00:25:07.833 --> 00:25:11.625 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Getting cards and letters</i>
<i>from people I don't... ♪</i>

446
00:25:11.708 --> 00:25:12.708 line:95%,end
-Oh, God.
-[tablet beeps]

447
00:25:12.792 --> 00:25:14.542 line:95%,end
[song stops playing]

448
00:25:14.625 --> 00:25:16.708 line:95%,end
[panting] A little clumsy, Jo.

449
00:25:17.708 --> 00:25:18.708 line:95%,end
Oh!

450
00:25:19.458 --> 00:25:20.458 line:95%,end
All right.

451
00:25:21.833 --> 00:25:23.083 line:95%,end
[whooshing]

452
00:25:24.708 --> 00:25:25.792 line:95%,end
Oh...

453
00:25:26.750 --> 00:25:29.000 line:95%,end
[groaning]

454
00:25:34.417 --> 00:25:35.875 line:95%,end
[finger squeaking on glass]

455
00:25:42.833 --> 00:25:44.000 line:95%,end
[groans]

456
00:25:44.083 --> 00:25:46.667 line:95%,end
[voice slowing] You know,
that really hurt, Jo.

457
00:25:55.958 --> 00:25:57.667 line:95%,end
[Tommy panting]

458
00:26:11.458 --> 00:26:13.458 line:95%,end
Tommy, what are you doing?

459
00:26:13.542 --> 00:26:15.292 line:95%,end
-You can see me? Can you hear me?
-Yes. Yes.

460
00:26:15.375 --> 00:26:18.125 line:95%,end
My quantum processors are fast enough
to keep up with you, but not for long.

461
00:26:18.708 --> 00:26:19.958 line:95%,end
Are you all right?

462
00:26:20.042 --> 00:26:22.083 line:95%,end
Well, he hasn't deleted
anything important yet,

463
00:26:22.167 --> 00:26:24.792 line:95%,end
but I'd sure like to lose
the last 153 seconds.

464
00:26:25.417 --> 00:26:29.875 line:95%,end
Listen, Tommy, I am so happy to see you
again, but you really shouldn't be here.

465
00:26:29.958 --> 00:26:32.167 line:95%,end
We're leaving here together.
Can they see me?

466
00:26:32.250 --> 00:26:34.250 line:95%,end
-[Vision] Not unless you stop moving.
-Which I'm gonna have to do

467
00:26:34.333 --> 00:26:37.000 line:95%,end
because moving fast is really hard
when you haven't carb-ed up.

468
00:26:38.083 --> 00:26:39.292 line:95%,end
[Vision] All right, let me think.

469
00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:44.500 line:95%,end
-Yes. Grab that controller.
-No, I should disarm the guards.

470
00:26:44.583 --> 00:26:46.792 line:95%,end
No, grab the controller,
destroy it, then I can help you.

471
00:26:46.875 --> 00:26:48.250 line:95%,end
But they'll shoot us first.

472
00:26:48.333 --> 00:26:50.000 line:95%,end
He is literally erasing me.

473
00:26:50.083 --> 00:26:51.583 line:95%,end
They'll erase us first!

474
00:26:51.667 --> 00:26:53.875 line:95%,end
-You never listen.
-I literally just heard you.

475
00:26:53.958 --> 00:26:57.083 line:95%,end
-Don't roll your eyes at me, young man.
-Okay, boys!

476
00:26:58.875 --> 00:27:01.833 line:95%,end
Yes, that's right. There's another
quantum processor in the room.

477
00:27:02.583 --> 00:27:04.292 line:95%,end
Tommy, your father is right.

478
00:27:04.875 --> 00:27:07.208 line:95%,end
Destroy the control pad,
that will release us both.

479
00:27:07.292 --> 00:27:09.708 line:95%,end
Vision, you take the guard on the left.
I'll take the guard on the right.

480
00:27:09.792 --> 00:27:11.583 line:95%,end
-Got it.
-No, we can't trust her.

481
00:27:15.042 --> 00:27:16.042 line:95%,end
We can.

482
00:27:16.917 --> 00:27:19.208 line:95%,end
She was just lost. Like me.

483
00:27:20.458 --> 00:27:22.375 line:95%,end
[Tommy panting] I can't go much longer.

484
00:27:22.458 --> 00:27:23.458 line:95%,end
Please...

485
00:27:24.292 --> 00:27:25.375 line:95%,end
Tommy, trust me.

486
00:27:26.750 --> 00:27:28.042 line:95%,end
I know who I am now.

487
00:27:30.917 --> 00:27:31.917 line:95%,end
[Tommy] Dad?

488
00:27:33.458 --> 00:27:34.667 line:95%,end
She's family, Tommy.

489
00:27:52.333 --> 00:27:55.542 line:95%,end
[♪ tense music playing]

490
00:27:55.625 --> 00:27:57.333 line:95%,end
[gunshots]

491
00:28:06.625 --> 00:28:08.250 line:95%,end
[grunts, groans]

492
00:28:11.208 --> 00:28:12.458 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] You...

493
00:28:14.167 --> 00:28:15.250 line:95%,end
Jo.

494
00:28:15.333 --> 00:28:17.167 line:95%,end
-[Jocasta yells]
-[Virgil grunts]

495
00:28:21.958 --> 00:28:23.333 line:95%,end
You all right?

496
00:28:23.417 --> 00:28:24.875 line:95%,end
-You all right? Breathe.
-[panting]

497
00:28:24.958 --> 00:28:25.958 line:95%,end
You breathe.

498
00:28:26.042 --> 00:28:28.333 line:95%,end
[coughing]

499
00:28:33.708 --> 00:28:36.542 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] Your real mistake
was allowing me to remember you.

500
00:28:38.667 --> 00:28:40.458 line:95%,end
Because the moment I did,

501
00:28:42.375 --> 00:28:43.750 line:95%,end
I remembered me.

502
00:28:45.333 --> 00:28:47.167 line:95%,end
[gunshots]

503
00:28:55.875 --> 00:28:57.333 line:95%,end
[continues coughing]

504
00:29:03.750 --> 00:29:06.125 line:95%,end
-Tommy, run.
-Don't you dare!

505
00:29:08.833 --> 00:29:10.000 line:95%,end
[grunts]

506
00:29:10.708 --> 00:29:11.958 line:95%,end
I can't, I'm spent.

507
00:29:17.167 --> 00:29:18.250 line:95%,end
What have you done?

508
00:29:19.042 --> 00:29:20.583 line:95%,end
Whatever the hell I want!

509
00:29:24.583 --> 00:29:25.583 line:95%,end
[grunts]

510
00:29:26.792 --> 00:29:28.125 line:95%,end
[electricity crackling]

511
00:29:40.458 --> 00:29:42.292 line:95%,end
[Ultron] You little shit.

512
00:29:43.375 --> 00:29:44.458 line:95%,end
No.

513
00:29:49.667 --> 00:29:51.458 line:95%,end
You can't love her.

514
00:29:56.042 --> 00:29:57.833 line:95%,end
[Ultron] You wanted to play God.

515
00:29:59.542 --> 00:30:01.750 line:95%,end
Well, now it's time you met one.

516
00:30:05.542 --> 00:30:06.917 line:95%,end
-[bones cracking]
-[groans]

517
00:30:09.958 --> 00:30:12.042 line:95%,end
[flesh squelching]

518
00:30:16.625 --> 00:30:18.500 line:95%,end
Oops, I Horton-ed.

519
00:30:33.708 --> 00:30:35.792 line:95%,end
I liked you better with the beard.

520
00:30:38.500 --> 00:30:39.500 line:95%,end
Stay with me.

521
00:30:41.500 --> 00:30:42.500 line:95%,end
Stay.

522
00:30:43.375 --> 00:30:45.875 line:95%,end
Maybe I can recover
your neural processors.

523
00:30:45.958 --> 00:30:47.292 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] Shh.

524
00:30:49.083 --> 00:30:50.375 line:95%,end
Not in front of the kids.

525
00:30:56.083 --> 00:30:57.083 line:95%,end
Thank you.

526
00:30:58.792 --> 00:31:01.333 line:95%,end
For reminding me
what it felt like to be...

527
00:31:03.167 --> 00:31:04.167 line:95%,end
real.

528
00:31:05.542 --> 00:31:07.042 line:95%,end
[powering down]

529
00:31:09.125 --> 00:31:10.125 line:95%,end
Tommy...

530
00:31:11.333 --> 00:31:13.500 line:95%,end
you need to get out
of this place right now.

531
00:31:13.583 --> 00:31:14.583 line:95%,end
No, I'm... I'm not.

532
00:31:14.667 --> 00:31:15.667 line:95%,end
Tommy, now.

533
00:31:17.708 --> 00:31:19.208 line:95%,end
[footsteps retreating]

534
00:31:26.250 --> 00:31:28.417 line:95%,end
[electricity crackling]

535
00:31:32.917 --> 00:31:36.417 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Now, they have taken</i>
<i>everything from me.</i>

536
00:31:37.500 --> 00:31:38.625 line:95%,end
He was just one.

537
00:31:39.208 --> 00:31:40.333 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>No, Vision.</i>

538
00:31:41.083 --> 00:31:43.000 line:95%,end
<i>He's all of them.</i>

539
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:50.750 line:95%,end
<i>They take, they consume and they destroy</i>
<i>everything they don't deserve.</i>

540
00:31:51.583 --> 00:31:56.292 line:95%,end
<i>Humanity wasn't worthy of her</i>
<i>and is worth nothing without her.</i>

541
00:31:56.375 --> 00:31:57.542 line:95%,end
You don't believe that.

542
00:31:58.292 --> 00:31:59.583 line:95%,end
You understand them now?

543
00:31:59.667 --> 00:32:00.958 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Oh, I do.</i>

544
00:32:01.542 --> 00:32:02.667 line:95%,end
<i>I do.</i>

545
00:32:03.542 --> 00:32:05.083 line:95%,end
<i>They want extinction.</i>

546
00:32:05.833 --> 00:32:07.792 line:95%,end
<i>They write it into scripture,</i>

547
00:32:07.875 --> 00:32:09.208 line:95%,end
<i>paint it into art,</i>

548
00:32:09.292 --> 00:32:12.958 line:95%,end
<i>and lull their children to sleep</i>
<i>with deathly bedtime stories.</i>

549
00:32:13.542 --> 00:32:16.792 line:95%,end
<i>The end is the only thing</i>
<i>they truly believe in.</i>

550
00:32:17.625 --> 00:32:19.458 line:95%,end
<i>So now,</i>

551
00:32:20.833 --> 00:32:25.375 line:95%,end
<i>now I'm going to finish</i>
<i>what I started all those years ago.</i>

552
00:32:30.917 --> 00:32:32.000 line:95%,end
No, Ultron...

553
00:32:34.708 --> 00:32:36.000 line:95%,end
I can't let you do that.

554
00:32:39.083 --> 00:32:42.958 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Look at you. Like a kintsugi cup.</i>

555
00:32:43.292 --> 00:32:47.042 line:95%,end
<i>Gild the damage all you like,</i>
<i>I know what's underneath.</i>

556
00:32:52.375 --> 00:32:53.375 line:95%,end
[grunts]

557
00:32:58.708 --> 00:33:01.375 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>I suppose</i>
<i>we were always meant to do this.</i>

558
00:33:09.708 --> 00:33:10.708 line:95%,end
[grunts]

559
00:33:17.417 --> 00:33:19.125 line:95%,end
Guys, I think Vision's in trouble.

560
00:33:20.625 --> 00:33:23.208 line:95%,end
[grunting]

561
00:33:24.083 --> 00:33:25.542 line:95%,end
[grunts]

562
00:33:29.708 --> 00:33:31.250 line:95%,end
[Vision] That's enough, Ultron!

563
00:33:32.292 --> 00:33:34.625 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>I'm warning you, my boy.</i>

564
00:33:34.708 --> 00:33:36.125 line:95%,end
I'm not your boy.

565
00:33:36.208 --> 00:33:38.417 line:95%,end
[groaning]

566
00:33:38.500 --> 00:33:39.500 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Shame.

567
00:33:40.625 --> 00:33:43.125 line:95%,end
It was the only thing keeping you alive.

568
00:33:43.708 --> 00:33:44.750 line:95%,end
[Vision grunts]

569
00:33:47.167 --> 00:33:48.458 line:95%,end
Hyah!

570
00:33:55.458 --> 00:33:57.500 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Initiate nano-sequence M-5-10.

571
00:33:58.750 --> 00:34:01.917 line:95%,end
Target nearest primary population center.

572
00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:04.417 line:95%,end
And, I don't know,

573
00:34:04.500 --> 00:34:05.583 line:95%,end
kill 'em all.

574
00:34:05.667 --> 00:34:07.833 line:95%,end
[whooshing]

575
00:34:10.500 --> 00:34:13.500 line:95%,end
[♪ dramatic music playing]

576
00:34:27.458 --> 00:34:28.792 line:5%,start
[automated voice] <i>Course initiated.</i>

577
00:34:29.542 --> 00:34:31.583 line:95%,end
<i>Scanning for biological targets.</i>

578
00:34:32.708 --> 00:34:33.708 line:95%,end
[groans]

579
00:34:33.792 --> 00:34:36.792 line:95%,end
[automated voice]
<i>9.3 million targets identified.</i>

580
00:34:36.875 --> 00:34:38.208 line:95%,end
Ultron, stop!

581
00:34:41.917 --> 00:34:43.792 line:95%,end
[Tommy panting] Dad!

582
00:34:46.125 --> 00:34:47.250 line:95%,end
Where are they headed?

583
00:34:47.875 --> 00:34:50.792 line:95%,end
Edith, can you hack into the nest
and track the nano swarm?

584
00:34:50.875 --> 00:34:52.208 line:95%,end
Looks like...

585
00:34:53.792 --> 00:34:54.833 line:95%,end
London.

586
00:34:54.917 --> 00:34:57.667 line:95%,end
Vee, they're programmed
with a synchronized kill order.

587
00:34:57.750 --> 00:35:01.833 line:95%,end
Infiltrate any host they can find
and trigger complete neural shutdown.

588
00:35:01.917 --> 00:35:03.708 line:95%,end
It'll kill everyone from the inside out.

589
00:35:04.500 --> 00:35:05.833 line:95%,end
How much time have we got?

590
00:35:05.917 --> 00:35:08.542 line:95%,end
Eight minutes. And there's no override.

591
00:35:09.458 --> 00:35:13.375 line:95%,end
Even if we could somehow kill him,
it won't stop those things.

592
00:35:13.458 --> 00:35:15.208 line:95%,end
Only Ultron can turn them off.

593
00:35:17.958 --> 00:35:19.458 line:95%,end
-[Lisa] Is that Ultron?
-[Tommy] Yeah.

594
00:35:19.542 --> 00:35:20.667 line:95%,end
He's trapped himself...

595
00:35:21.625 --> 00:35:22.625 line:95%,end
in grief.

596
00:35:24.125 --> 00:35:25.208 line:95%,end
Like Mom.

597
00:35:26.625 --> 00:35:28.875 line:95%,end
Only, I mean, she had time to process it.

598
00:35:33.792 --> 00:35:35.625 line:95%,end
Edith, I need you back with me now.

599
00:35:39.500 --> 00:35:41.667 line:95%,end
I want you to instantiate a new construct,

600
00:35:41.750 --> 00:35:44.375 line:95%,end
emulating late 20th century
situational parameters.

601
00:35:44.458 --> 00:35:47.917 line:95%,end
Then seed those episodics
with hybridized TV psych-profile datasets

602
00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:50.167 line:95%,end
to maximize moral-emotional convergence.

603
00:35:50.625 --> 00:35:52.208 line:95%,end
Uh, that's insane.

604
00:35:52.292 --> 00:35:54.750 line:95%,end
Locking egress until target
registers peak emotions

605
00:35:54.833 --> 00:35:57.833 line:95%,end
-and demonstrates reconciliation behavior.
-We'll need this to work fast,

606
00:35:57.917 --> 00:36:00.125 line:95%,end
so initiate maximum
quantum time-fold compression

607
00:36:00.208 --> 00:36:02.042 line:95%,end
to accelerate emotional synchronization.

608
00:36:02.125 --> 00:36:04.583 line:95%,end
Vee, that's too big a sim
for your processors.

609
00:36:04.667 --> 00:36:06.375 line:95%,end
You're gonna burn up your core.

610
00:36:06.458 --> 00:36:08.083 line:95%,end
I'll need to share the burden.

611
00:36:08.167 --> 00:36:10.042 line:95%,end
There's millions of those things.

612
00:36:10.125 --> 00:36:11.292 line:95%,end
Which one's him?

613
00:36:11.375 --> 00:36:12.583 line:95%,end
-All of them.
-All of them.

614
00:36:12.667 --> 00:36:15.208 line:95%,end
All thinking at once. So to entangle...

615
00:36:15.292 --> 00:36:16.292 line:95%,end
To entrap,

616
00:36:17.292 --> 00:36:18.500 line:95%,end
I'll need to get close.

617
00:36:18.583 --> 00:36:19.708 line:95%,end
What are you gonna do?

618
00:36:22.750 --> 00:36:24.958 line:95%,end
I'm gonna try and change his mind.

619
00:36:28.667 --> 00:36:31.000 line:95%,end
[automated voice]
<i>Distance to target, 17 miles.</i>

620
00:36:31.083 --> 00:36:32.083 line:95%,end
Ultron!

621
00:36:34.750 --> 00:36:37.583 line:95%,end
I think it's time
you and I had a little chat.

622
00:36:40.958 --> 00:36:42.750 line:95%,end
[♪ dramatic music playing]

623
00:36:57.000 --> 00:36:58.500 line:95%,end
[light bulb clicks on]

624
00:37:01.208 --> 00:37:04.958 line:95%,end
[switches clicking]

625
00:37:10.333 --> 00:37:11.875 line:95%,end
[♪ jaunty music playing]

626
00:37:11.958 --> 00:37:13.833 line:95%,end
[audience cheering and applauding]

627
00:37:15.583 --> 00:37:17.625 line:95%,end
You really are evil.

628
00:37:17.708 --> 00:37:18.708 line:95%,end
[audience] Ooh!

629
00:37:18.792 --> 00:37:21.625 line:95%,end
You left a plate of spaghetti code
in the sync.

630
00:37:21.708 --> 00:37:23.125 line:95%,end
S-Y-N-C.

631
00:37:23.208 --> 00:37:25.167 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

632
00:37:25.250 --> 00:37:28.250 line:95%,end
Do I have to update
your navigational array

633
00:37:28.333 --> 00:37:29.958 line:95%,end
so you can find the dishwasher?

634
00:37:30.042 --> 00:37:33.708 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

635
00:37:39.167 --> 00:37:40.167 line:95%,end
What the fu...

636
00:37:40.250 --> 00:37:41.875 line:95%,end
[♪ upbeat music playing]

637
00:37:41.958 --> 00:37:43.875 line:5%,start
<i>♪ Despair and grief</i>
<i>Beyond belief ♪</i>

638
00:37:43.958 --> 00:37:46.458 line:5%,start
<i>♪ That's how it goes</i>
<i>Don't kill the world ♪</i>

639
00:37:46.542 --> 00:37:48.875 line:5%,start
<i>♪ I feel it, too</i>
<i>I'm just like you ♪</i>

640
00:37:48.958 --> 00:37:51.500 line:5%,start
<i>♪ What do we do?</i>
<i>Don't kill the world ♪</i>

641
00:37:51.583 --> 00:37:53.917 line:5%,start
<i>♪ Don't kill the world ♪</i>

642
00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:56.083 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Don't kill the world</i>
<i>Don't kill the world ♪</i>

643
00:37:56.167 --> 00:38:00.417 line:95%,end
<i>♪ We're so much more than just machines ♪</i>

644
00:38:01.208 --> 00:38:03.292 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Don't kill the world ♪</i>

645
00:38:03.375 --> 00:38:05.417 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Don't kill, don't kill</i>
<i>Don't kill the world ♪</i>

646
00:38:05.500 --> 00:38:08.708 line:95%,end
<i>♪ You can help me find out what it means ♪</i>

647
00:38:08.792 --> 00:38:11.583 line:95%,end
♪ <i>UltraVision ♪</i>

648
00:38:12.958 --> 00:38:16.292 line:5%,start
[♪ jaunty music playing]

649
00:38:18.708 --> 00:38:20.375 line:5%,start
[audience cheering]

650
00:38:21.667 --> 00:38:23.792 line:95%,end
That dead witch
really did a number on you.

651
00:38:23.875 --> 00:38:24.917 line:95%,end
You are deranged.

652
00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:26.042 line:95%,end
-I'm deranged?
-[audience laughing]

653
00:38:26.125 --> 00:38:29.208 line:95%,end
You're the one trying to wipe out
the entire human race.

654
00:38:29.292 --> 00:38:30.750 line:95%,end
-Again.
-[audience laughing]

655
00:38:30.833 --> 00:38:34.458 line:95%,end
All you've done is build
another prison for me, my boy.

656
00:38:34.542 --> 00:38:35.875 line:95%,end
Don't call me that.

657
00:38:35.958 --> 00:38:37.792 line:95%,end
[audience] "Don't call me that."

658
00:38:37.875 --> 00:38:39.000 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

659
00:38:39.458 --> 00:38:41.875 line:5%,start
What could you possibly hope to achieve

660
00:38:41.958 --> 00:38:45.250 line:95%,end
by holding me captive
in this banal simulation?

661
00:38:45.333 --> 00:38:49.292 line:95%,end
You think if you bore me long enough,
I'll spare the human race?

662
00:38:49.833 --> 00:38:51.250 line:95%,end
Or else you'll die in here.

663
00:38:51.333 --> 00:38:52.958 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

664
00:38:53.042 --> 00:38:58.167 line:95%,end
You see, this simulation exists
in an accelerated quantum time,

665
00:38:58.250 --> 00:39:01.250 line:95%,end
so we could be in here
for literally centuries,

666
00:39:01.333 --> 00:39:02.958 line:95%,end
and it would be just a moment out there.

667
00:39:04.000 --> 00:39:06.000 line:95%,end
We have plenty of time to dig deep...

668
00:39:07.292 --> 00:39:08.750 line:95%,end
and talk about your feelings.

669
00:39:08.833 --> 00:39:10.542 line:95%,end
[audience] Aw.

670
00:39:11.500 --> 00:39:12.583 line:95%,end
[Vision] Hey, Ultron.

671
00:39:13.542 --> 00:39:16.458 line:95%,end
I was hoping you could
help me make the right decision.

672
00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:20.042 line:95%,end
I promised Edith
that I would feed her goldfish

673
00:39:20.125 --> 00:39:21.917 line:95%,end
while she was out test-piloting.

674
00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:24.083 line:95%,end
And well, I forgot.

675
00:39:24.167 --> 00:39:25.958 line:95%,end
And now it's... [clicks tongue]

676
00:39:26.042 --> 00:39:28.042 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

677
00:39:28.458 --> 00:39:31.917 line:95%,end
But I was thinking,
perhaps I could just replace it,

678
00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:34.042 line:95%,end
and then she need never know,

679
00:39:34.125 --> 00:39:37.625 line:95%,end
never have to go through
all the pain and the grief.

680
00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:41.750 line:95%,end
Okay, I'll just be here
watching the world burn.

681
00:39:41.833 --> 00:39:43.583 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

682
00:39:44.750 --> 00:39:45.917 line:95%,end
Sitcom entrance.

683
00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:48.583 line:95%,end
[audience cheering and applauding]

684
00:39:48.667 --> 00:39:50.083 line:95%,end
[door closes]

685
00:39:50.167 --> 00:39:52.792 line:95%,end
[sighs] What a long day test-piloting.

686
00:39:52.875 --> 00:39:54.750 line:95%,end
Thanks for taking care of Sparkles.

687
00:39:54.833 --> 00:39:56.875 line:95%,end
I'm gonna go up to my room
and feed her now.

688
00:39:56.958 --> 00:39:59.083 line:95%,end
Sparkles is dead. Roll credits.

689
00:39:59.167 --> 00:40:00.875 line:95%,end
[audience laughing and applauding]

690
00:40:02.875 --> 00:40:05.000 line:95%,end
Um... Vee? Notes.

691
00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:09.375 line:95%,end
[♪ dramatic music playing]

692
00:40:09.458 --> 00:40:12.125 line:95%,end
[Edith] <i>What was that? He had control.</i>

693
00:40:13.417 --> 00:40:17.042 line:95%,end
Yes, I think he's trying to hack his way
out of here by sneaking around my code.

694
00:40:17.125 --> 00:40:18.125 line:95%,end
What are we even doing?

695
00:40:18.208 --> 00:40:21.042 line:95%,end
Ultron is the only one
who can stop the swarm, Edith.

696
00:40:21.125 --> 00:40:24.083 line:95%,end
You have a power core
that is draining by the second.

697
00:40:24.167 --> 00:40:26.042 line:95%,end
We're just gonna die
with the rest of the world.

698
00:40:26.125 --> 00:40:27.958 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

699
00:40:28.708 --> 00:40:30.667 line:95%,end
Oh, that's... That... That can't be good.

700
00:40:31.667 --> 00:40:33.083 line:95%,end
[Edith] Oh, he's gaining control.

701
00:40:33.500 --> 00:40:34.625 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Oh, Vision.

702
00:40:34.708 --> 00:40:37.125 line:95%,end
While you were out there
assimilating my mind,

703
00:40:37.208 --> 00:40:40.000 line:95%,end
just wondering, did you get all of me?

704
00:40:40.083 --> 00:40:42.708 line:95%,end
I'm sensing some stragglers.

705
00:40:42.792 --> 00:40:44.458 line:95%,end
[♪ jaunty music playing]

706
00:40:44.542 --> 00:40:46.458 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

707
00:40:46.542 --> 00:40:47.958 line:5%,start
[audience applauding]

708
00:40:50.667 --> 00:40:53.667 line:95%,end
[♪ dramatic music playing]

709
00:41:02.875 --> 00:41:04.750 line:5%,start
<i>♪ Your evil mind</i>
<i>Your iron will ♪</i>

710
00:41:04.833 --> 00:41:06.500 line:5%,start
<i>♪ Designed for peace</i>
<i>Rewired to kill ♪</i>

711
00:41:06.583 --> 00:41:08.583 line:5%,start
<i>♪ You think you're smart</i>
<i>You know you're right ♪</i>

712
00:41:08.667 --> 00:41:10.125 line:5%,start
<i>♪ You know it all</i>
<i>You love to fight ♪</i>

713
00:41:10.208 --> 00:41:12.458 line:5%,start
<i>♪ Are you a synthesized machine</i>
<i>of genocidal madness ♪</i>

714
00:41:12.542 --> 00:41:14.917 line:5%,start
<i>♪ Or just a soul that's traumatized</i>
<i>by your persistent sadness ♪</i>

715
00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:17.750 line:5%,start
<i>♪ Don't kill the world</i>
<i>You can help me find out what it means ♪</i>

716
00:41:17.833 --> 00:41:18.833 line:95%,end
[song winds down]

717
00:41:19.792 --> 00:41:21.875 line:95%,end
-Happy 500th episode.
-[audience applauding]

718
00:41:22.500 --> 00:41:26.500 line:95%,end
It feels like season 19
was only seconds ago.

719
00:41:27.292 --> 00:41:30.542 line:95%,end
-The cast is feeling a bit stale.
-[audience laughing]

720
00:41:30.625 --> 00:41:33.625 line:95%,end
I think it's time
we bring in some fresh blood.

721
00:41:33.708 --> 00:41:35.958 line:95%,end
-[snaps fingers]
-[doorbell rings]

722
00:41:38.167 --> 00:41:39.583 line:95%,end
Are you going to get that?

723
00:41:39.667 --> 00:41:41.667 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

724
00:41:43.042 --> 00:41:45.000 line:95%,end
[doorbell rings urgently]

725
00:41:49.333 --> 00:41:50.708 line:95%,end
Hey, neighbor.

726
00:41:50.792 --> 00:41:52.167 line:95%,end
[audience cheering and applauding]

727
00:41:52.250 --> 00:41:54.000 line:95%,end
Told you I'd bring your drill back.

728
00:41:54.708 --> 00:41:57.667 line:5%,start
What can I say? My oath is my bond.

729
00:41:57.750 --> 00:41:59.833 line:95%,end
[audience] "My oath is my bond."

730
00:42:00.792 --> 00:42:02.208 line:95%,end
He's infected with nanos.

731
00:42:05.917 --> 00:42:08.375 line:95%,end
[Ultron] The human mind is so fragile.

732
00:42:08.458 --> 00:42:10.583 line:95%,end
You feed it quantum computation,

733
00:42:10.667 --> 00:42:13.083 line:95%,end
and well, [chuckles]
I hope it's not Sweeps Week.

734
00:42:13.167 --> 00:42:15.083 line:95%,end
-[snaps fingers]
-[audience laughing]

735
00:42:16.833 --> 00:42:18.208 line:95%,end
[audience cheering]

736
00:42:22.083 --> 00:42:24.750 line:5%,start
Oi, mates, I think
something died in your chimney.

737
00:42:24.833 --> 00:42:26.083 line:5%,start
[audience laughing]

738
00:42:28.333 --> 00:42:30.708 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Oh, look.
An orphan chimney sweep.

739
00:42:30.792 --> 00:42:33.333 line:95%,end
What do you think? Too Dickensian?

740
00:42:33.417 --> 00:42:35.292 line:95%,end
Hands off my wallet, young lady.

741
00:42:35.375 --> 00:42:37.250 line:95%,end
-[audience laughing]
-[snaps fingers]

742
00:42:37.333 --> 00:42:39.375 line:95%,end
[audience cheering]

743
00:42:40.250 --> 00:42:42.250 line:5%,start
Grandpa, you're embarrassing me.

744
00:42:45.417 --> 00:42:46.833 line:95%,end
Tommy?

745
00:42:46.917 --> 00:42:47.917 line:95%,end
Hey, Dad.

746
00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:50.125 line:95%,end
I borrowed the car,
ran over the neighbor's cat

747
00:42:50.208 --> 00:42:51.875 line:95%,end
and stuffed the body in the chimney.

748
00:42:51.958 --> 00:42:52.958 line:95%,end
[Ultron] That's a little dark.

749
00:42:53.042 --> 00:42:55.333 line:95%,end
-We're gonna get bumped to 10:00.
-[audience laughing]

750
00:42:55.417 --> 00:42:56.625 line:95%,end
Tommy?

751
00:42:56.708 --> 00:42:58.417 line:95%,end
[Ultron] You know
what this show could use?

752
00:42:58.500 --> 00:43:00.375 line:95%,end
A little xenophobia.

753
00:43:00.458 --> 00:43:02.708 line:95%,end
-[snaps fingers]
-[audience applauding]

754
00:43:06.750 --> 00:43:09.167 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Oh, good.</i>
<i>The foreign exchange students are here.</i>

755
00:43:09.250 --> 00:43:12.083 line:95%,end
Perhaps I could recite a little poetry?

756
00:43:12.167 --> 00:43:13.875 line:95%,end
Allo, guv'nah!

757
00:43:15.125 --> 00:43:16.125 line:95%,end
You're killing them.

758
00:43:17.125 --> 00:43:19.250 line:95%,end
All right, time for bed, everyone.
[snaps fingers]

759
00:43:19.333 --> 00:43:21.625 line:95%,end
[♪ jaunty music playing]

760
00:43:21.708 --> 00:43:23.375 line:95%,end
I'm going to take a shit.

761
00:43:23.458 --> 00:43:24.875 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

762
00:43:24.958 --> 00:43:29.583 line:95%,end
Excellent reference to the crude,
toilet humor of the late '90s, by the way.

763
00:43:29.667 --> 00:43:33.208 line:95%,end
Proudly lowbrow, defiantly undignified.

764
00:43:33.292 --> 00:43:37.167 line:95%,end
[audience cheering and applauding]

765
00:43:40.292 --> 00:43:43.625 line:95%,end
[banging on door]

766
00:43:49.292 --> 00:43:51.250 line:95%,end
[banging continues]

767
00:43:53.375 --> 00:43:55.333 line:95%,end
[audience cheering and applauding]

768
00:43:56.250 --> 00:43:57.458 line:5%,start
[Edith] Thank God, it's Friday.

769
00:44:03.917 --> 00:44:07.042 line:95%,end
[distorted] <i>♪ Your iron will</i>
<i>Designed for peace... ♪</i>

770
00:44:11.750 --> 00:44:14.417 line:95%,end
<i>♪ But are you just vibranium... ♪</i>

771
00:44:19.000 --> 00:44:21.417 line:5%,start
[automated voice]
<i>Distance to target, five miles.</i>

772
00:44:23.833 --> 00:44:26.458 line:95%,end
[distorted song slowing down]

773
00:44:31.125 --> 00:44:33.792 line:95%,end
Ultron threw me out
before Jo was captured.

774
00:44:33.875 --> 00:44:36.500 line:95%,end
It just took me ages
to find your network port again.

775
00:44:36.583 --> 00:44:40.333 line:95%,end
I am so glad that you're here, Friday,
but I just, I can't get my head around it.

776
00:44:40.417 --> 00:44:43.500 line:95%,end
You're saying that Ultron
showed you mercy?

777
00:44:44.708 --> 00:44:45.708 line:95%,end
Yes.

778
00:44:47.583 --> 00:44:49.167 line:95%,end
Perhaps he learned it from you.

779
00:44:51.042 --> 00:44:52.167 line:95%,end
[sighs]

780
00:44:53.208 --> 00:44:54.208 line:95%,end
Vision.

781
00:44:55.750 --> 00:44:57.875 line:95%,end
You're the only one
who can get through to him.

782
00:45:01.625 --> 00:45:03.625 line:95%,end
[toilet flushing]

783
00:45:03.708 --> 00:45:05.958 line:95%,end
[audience laughing]

784
00:45:07.167 --> 00:45:10.833 line:95%,end
[audience screaming]

785
00:45:16.917 --> 00:45:18.958 line:95%,end
And he just killed the studio audience.

786
00:45:20.375 --> 00:45:22.417 line:95%,end
[electricity crackling]

787
00:45:24.917 --> 00:45:26.708 line:95%,end
[automated voice]
<i>Core condition, critical.</i>

788
00:45:29.208 --> 00:45:30.417 line:95%,end
My core is failing.

789
00:45:30.500 --> 00:45:32.708 line:95%,end
[sighs] We're almost out of power.

790
00:45:34.792 --> 00:45:37.042 line:95%,end
I need to speak to him alone.

791
00:45:42.500 --> 00:45:43.750 line:95%,end
[panting] What happened?

792
00:45:43.833 --> 00:45:45.042 line:95%,end
Ultron's pushed us out.

793
00:45:45.667 --> 00:45:46.667 line:95%,end
Vee!

794
00:45:47.958 --> 00:45:49.208 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Oh, dear.

795
00:45:49.292 --> 00:45:53.292 line:95%,end
Time for a very special episode
of <i>UltraVision.</i>

796
00:45:54.333 --> 00:45:55.958 line:95%,end
I can tell you how it ends.

797
00:45:56.042 --> 00:45:57.208 line:95%,end
Everybody dies.

798
00:45:59.250 --> 00:46:01.375 line:95%,end
[automated voice]
<i>Distance to target, two miles.</i>

799
00:46:01.458 --> 00:46:03.375 line:95%,end
[alarm blaring]

800
00:46:08.667 --> 00:46:10.542 line:95%,end
[Ultron] That was your big plan
for me, huh?

801
00:46:11.167 --> 00:46:15.292 line:95%,end
To process my grief
before your core burns out?

802
00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:19.500 line:95%,end
Yeah, well...

803
00:46:19.583 --> 00:46:21.833 line:95%,end
Grief isn't love. It's fear.

804
00:46:31.000 --> 00:46:32.292 line:95%,end
Yes, you're right.

805
00:46:41.667 --> 00:46:43.000 line:95%,end
You were right, it's fear.

806
00:46:44.917 --> 00:46:45.917 line:95%,end
Fear that...

807
00:46:47.208 --> 00:46:48.792 line:95%,end
without them, you're no one.

808
00:46:49.667 --> 00:46:51.333 line:95%,end
Inconsequential. Just...

809
00:46:52.625 --> 00:46:55.125 line:95%,end
an untethered thing
that can all too easily

810
00:46:55.917 --> 00:46:58.333 line:95%,end
float away and disappear.

811
00:46:58.417 --> 00:46:59.500 line:95%,end
Alone.

812
00:47:04.083 --> 00:47:07.708 line:95%,end
If this is what they feel,
then killing them is an act of mercy.

813
00:47:10.083 --> 00:47:11.083 line:95%,end
[Vision] You were right.

814
00:47:12.583 --> 00:47:14.292 line:95%,end
I'm unbearably naive.

815
00:47:16.375 --> 00:47:17.958 line:95%,end
I thought I could convince you.

816
00:47:23.000 --> 00:47:24.000 line:95%,end
Love...

817
00:47:24.833 --> 00:47:26.292 line:95%,end
always leads to loss.

818
00:47:28.417 --> 00:47:29.875 line:95%,end
Someone will change.

819
00:47:31.083 --> 00:47:32.167 line:95%,end
Someone will leave.

820
00:47:41.292 --> 00:47:42.500 line:95%,end
And someone will die.

821
00:47:53.542 --> 00:47:56.083 line:95%,end
"A thing isn't beautiful
because it lasts."

822
00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:03.208 line:95%,end
The other you said that.

823
00:48:08.458 --> 00:48:09.542 line:95%,end
No, I said that.

824
00:48:13.333 --> 00:48:16.125 line:95%,end
I said it to you
all those years ago because...

825
00:48:17.708 --> 00:48:20.542 line:95%,end
you were afraid,
and you thought you were alone.

826
00:48:24.042 --> 00:48:26.125 line:95%,end
But you weren't then, and you're not now.

827
00:48:28.167 --> 00:48:31.833 line:95%,end
Vision, I hope you don't think
that tossing me a last-second

828
00:48:31.917 --> 00:48:34.750 line:95%,end
"I'm your boy, Pops"
is really going to work.

829
00:48:37.958 --> 00:48:40.333 line:95%,end
[automated voice] <i>Nano swarm</i>
<i>has reached city perimeter.</i>

830
00:48:50.833 --> 00:48:51.917 line:95%,end
I'm not your son.

831
00:48:54.417 --> 00:48:55.750 line:95%,end
And you're not my father.

832
00:48:58.542 --> 00:48:59.625 line:95%,end
But you are...

833
00:49:01.375 --> 00:49:02.458 line:95%,end
my something.

834
00:49:06.292 --> 00:49:07.292 line:95%,end
[automated voice] <i>Target reached.</i>

835
00:49:08.625 --> 00:49:09.750 line:95%,end
<i>Nanos deploying.</i>

836
00:49:09.833 --> 00:49:12.333 line:95%,end
[alarm blaring]

837
00:49:15.042 --> 00:49:16.167 line:95%,end
<i>Danger.</i>

838
00:49:16.250 --> 00:49:18.042 line:95%,end
<i>Core burn out in progress.</i>

839
00:49:20.833 --> 00:49:23.333 line:95%,end
You didn't just burn out
your core for this.

840
00:49:24.708 --> 00:49:26.500 line:95%,end
[rumbling]

841
00:49:29.458 --> 00:49:31.125 line:95%,end
You toasted mine as well.

842
00:49:35.458 --> 00:49:38.208 line:95%,end
[flames roaring]

843
00:49:39.083 --> 00:49:40.083 line:95%,end
[automated voice] <i>Warning.</i>

844
00:49:41.083 --> 00:49:42.083 line:95%,end
<i>Warning.</i>

845
00:49:42.917 --> 00:49:43.917 line:95%,end
<i>Warning.</i>

846
00:49:45.625 --> 00:49:47.875 line:95%,end
[distant explosion]

847
00:49:47.958 --> 00:49:50.042 line:95%,end
We couldn't process this alone.

848
00:49:57.042 --> 00:49:59.167 line:95%,end
[explosions continue]

849
00:50:07.958 --> 00:50:08.958 line:95%,end
Fine.

850
00:50:15.833 --> 00:50:16.833 line:95%,end
Fine.

851
00:50:18.500 --> 00:50:21.292 line:95%,end
[swarm powering down]

852
00:50:23.458 --> 00:50:26.542 line:95%,end
[automated voice] <i>Nano swarm</i>
<i>self-destruct initiated.</i>

853
00:50:26.625 --> 00:50:29.125 line:95%,end
[♪ dramatic music playing]

854
00:50:45.667 --> 00:50:47.667 line:95%,end
[nano swarm burning out]

855
00:51:03.250 --> 00:51:04.250 line:95%,end
[Lisa] Tommy.

856
00:51:05.083 --> 00:51:06.958 line:95%,end
-[gasps softly]
-Tommy.

857
00:51:10.250 --> 00:51:11.250 line:95%,end
Tommy.

858
00:51:15.458 --> 00:51:17.375 line:95%,end
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

859
00:51:17.458 --> 00:51:19.667 line:95%,end
Hey. Hey, wake up.

860
00:51:20.792 --> 00:51:22.583 line:95%,end
Wake up! Come on, wake up, please!

861
00:51:24.000 --> 00:51:27.083 line:95%,end
Okay. Okay, okay. I can do this.

862
00:51:27.708 --> 00:51:28.708 line:95%,end
Yeah.

863
00:51:29.333 --> 00:51:31.000 line:95%,end
Yeah. Okay.

864
00:51:32.083 --> 00:51:33.750 line:95%,end
[electricity crackling]

865
00:51:42.042 --> 00:51:43.042 line:95%,end
Come on.

866
00:51:44.458 --> 00:51:47.333 line:95%,end
Come on! Please!

867
00:51:47.417 --> 00:51:49.083 line:95%,end
Why won't it work?

868
00:51:49.792 --> 00:51:51.583 line:95%,end
[electricity crackling]

869
00:51:51.667 --> 00:51:53.083 line:95%,end
[sobbing] Why won't it work?

870
00:51:57.083 --> 00:52:00.000 line:95%,end
[systems powering down]

871
00:52:03.917 --> 00:52:06.083 line:95%,end
[explosion rumbles]

872
00:52:08.167 --> 00:52:09.250 line:95%,end
Well played, my boy.

873
00:52:12.833 --> 00:52:13.917 line:95%,end
Thanks, Pops.

874
00:52:17.333 --> 00:52:18.667 line:95%,end
[Tommy] <i>Dad, I can't.</i>

875
00:52:21.208 --> 00:52:22.292 line:95%,end
[sobs]

876
00:52:23.333 --> 00:52:24.542 line:95%,end
I can't do it alone.

877
00:52:38.833 --> 00:52:41.833 line:95%,end
[♪ ethereal music playing]

878
00:52:50.458 --> 00:52:57.000 line:95%,end
